{% comment %}
  Standard content page — FAQs, the four policies, About Us. On the live
  site (2026-08-04 captures in audit/screenshots/) every one of these
  pages is breadcrumbs + a 1200x400 CMS banner graphic (about-us: 1200x600
  photo) + the CMS HTML body, with no on-page text <h1>.

  Banner: the image picker wins when set; otherwise banner_asset names a
  file shipped in assets/ (the six live banners were downloaded there as
  page-banner-<handle>.jpg, and templates/page.<handle>.json pre-wires
  each). When a banner renders, the title drops to sr-only — the live
  pages never show a text title. With neither set, the italic text title
  shows (templates/page.json, the default, ships that way).

  The body renders from page.content so Min edits it in the admin.
  Cleaned body HTML for the six migrated pages is in
  docs/policy-page-content/. The page-body--<handle> class scopes the
  per-page typography variants measured from the live pages (see the
  Content pages block in akdy.css).
{% endcomment %}

<div class="container">
  {% render 'breadcrumbs' %}

  <article class="page">
    {%- if section.settings.banner_image -%}
      {{ section.settings.banner_image | image_url: width: 2280 | image_tag: class: 'page-banner', alt: '' }}
      <h1 class="page-title sr-only">{{ page.title }}</h1>
    {%- elsif section.settings.banner_asset != blank -%}
      <img class="page-banner" src="{{ section.settings.banner_asset | asset_url }}" alt=""
           width="{{ section.settings.banner_asset_width | default: 1200 }}"
           height="{{ section.settings.banner_asset_height | default: 400 }}">
      <h1 class="page-title sr-only">{{ page.title }}</h1>
    {%- else -%}
      <h1 class="page-title">{{ page.title }}</h1>
    {%- endif -%}
    <div class="page-body page-body--{{ page.handle }}">
      {{ page.content }}
    </div>
  </article>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Page",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "banner_image",
      "label": "Banner image",
      "info": "Shown above the content instead of the text title. Leave unset for a plain titled page."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "banner_asset",
      "label": "Banner asset filename",
      "info": "Fallback when no banner image is picked: the name of a file in the theme's assets folder, e.g. page-banner-faqs.jpg. The captured live banners ship there."
    },
    {
      "type": "number",
      "id": "banner_asset_width",
      "label": "Banner asset width (px)",
      "default": 1200,
      "info": "Intrinsic size of the asset file, for layout stability. The captured banners are 1200x400 (about-us: 1200x600)."
    },
    {
      "type": "number",
      "id": "banner_asset_height",
      "label": "Banner asset height (px)",
      "default": 400
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
